# Production builds talk to their own origin (DR-0041 decision 3): seedpod serves
# this bundle itself, so there is no second port and no cross-origin API URL.
#
# This file exists to OVERRIDE a developer's `ui/.env`, which is gitignored and
# on at least one machine says `VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000` for the vite
# dev-server workflow. `vite build` runs in mode=production and loads
# `.env.production` at higher priority than `.env`, so the dev value cannot leak
# into a release. It leaked once: the 2026-08-15 artifact shipped a bundle that
# sent every request to localhost:8000, which works perfectly on the server host
# and fails for every other client -- login "failed with that key" from a laptop,
# because the request never reached the appliance at all.
#
# Empty is meaningful: api-client.js and sse-client.js both do
# `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || ''`, and an empty base means same-origin.
VITE_API_URL=
